# Built-in Wazuh rules the lessons rely on, plus the lab's sudo-group rule.
# If an upgrade changes one of these, the lessons' answer keys need updating.

[invalid SSH user]
log: Oct 11 21:41:10 linux-srv sshd[2345]: Invalid user admin from 10.0.1.10 port 40122
rule: 5710
level: 5
field: srcip=10.0.1.10

[eight invalid users become a brute force]
log: Oct 11 21:41:10 linux-srv sshd[2345]: Invalid user admin from 10.0.1.10 port 40122
repeat: 8
rule: 5712
level: 10

[wrong password for a real user]
log: Oct 11 21:42:05 linux-srv sshd[2350]: Failed password for labuser from 10.0.1.10 port 40130 ssh2
rule: 5760
level: 5

[eight wrong passwords become a brute force]
log: Oct 11 21:42:05 linux-srv sshd[2350]: Failed password for labuser from 10.0.1.10 port 40130 ssh2
repeat: 8
rule: 5763
level: 10

[key login succeeds]
log: Oct 12 06:14:30 linux-srv sshd[10460]: Accepted publickey for azureuser from 10.0.1.20 port 50111 ssh2: ED25519 SHA256:abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEFG
rule: 5715
level: 3
field: srcip=10.0.1.20

[connection reset before login is a low alert]
log: Oct 12 06:14:27 linux-srv sshd[10456]: Connection reset by authenticating user labuser 10.0.1.10 port 57179 [preauth]
rule: 5762
level: 4

[connection closed before login is NOT an alert (level 0)]
log: Oct 12 06:14:26 linux-srv sshd[10455]: Connection closed by authenticating user labuser 10.0.1.10 port 57178 [preauth]
rule: 5722
level: 0

[sudo command]
log: Oct 12 06:14:40 linux-srv sudo[10470]: azureuser : TTY=pts/0 ; PWD=/home/azureuser ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/ls
log: Oct 12 06:14:41 linux-srv sudo[10471]: azureuser : TTY=pts/0 ; PWD=/home/azureuser ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/ls
rule: 5402
level: 3
field: srcuser=azureuser
field: command=/usr/bin/ls

[first sudo by an account]
log: Oct 12 06:14:40 linux-srv sudo[10470]: azureuser : TTY=pts/0 ; PWD=/home/azureuser ; USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/ls
rule: 5403
level: 4

[new Linux user]
log: Oct 11 21:43:00 linux-srv useradd[2400]: new user: name=svc_backup, UID=1002, GID=1002, home=/home/svc_backup, shell=/bin/bash, from=/dev/pts/0
rule: 5902
level: 8

[user added to sudo is raised by the lab rule]
log: Oct 11 21:43:05 linux-srv gpasswd[2410]: user svc_backup added by kt to group sudo
rule: 100110
level: 10

[user deleted]
log: Oct 11 21:50:00 linux-srv userdel[2500]: delete user 'svc_backup'
rule: 5903
level: 3
